  "verbalization": "Certonardosterol J is implicated in the interaction with HPAC through a series of molecular targets, primarily the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is targeted by multiple compounds, including Certonardosterol J, Paeonianin E, and Nordextrorphan, all of which ultimately lead to a shared interaction with HPAC. The evidence suggests a pathway where Certonardosterol J may influence the function of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which in turn affects HPAC. The consistent presence of HPAC as a target across these pathways implies a potential role for Certonardosterol J in modulating the activity of this transporter, possibly through a mechanism involving ion transport or cellular signaling. The overlapping targets and the presence of multiple compounds that share this interaction highlight a possible functional link between Certonardosterol J and HPAC, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
